;
; TicMambo configuration.
;
; Format: Keyword Value. Keywords are case insensitive.
; Lines starting with ';' or '#' are comments.
; Periods are whole days. Yes/No are boolean values.
; The file is read as UTF-8 or, if it is not valid UTF-8, in the system
; encoding (the ANSI code page on Windows).
;

TicPath d:\fido\inbound
;
; Where to look for tics. Required.

;FilesPath d:\fido\inbound
;
; Where to look for files. Default: TicPath.
; Besides the file named in the tic, its copies renamed by the mailer
; (file.zip.1, file.zi0 and so on) are checked too. A matching copy is
; moved to DestPath under the name from the tic.

DestPath d:\fido\inbound\fecho
;
; Where to move files together with their tics. Required. Must be
; different from TicPath and FilesPath.
; Set this directory as the inbound in your file echo processor's config.

;TicCharset cp866
;
; Encoding of file names in tics. Names are converted from it to the file
; system encoding. Default: cp866.

;FileNamesCaseSensitive Yes
;
; Yes - the file of a tic and its renamed copies must have the same case
; as the name in the tic. No - case is ignored. This does not depend on
; the file system: on Windows too, Yes means FILE.ZIP in a tic does not
; match file.zip. Default: No on Windows, Yes elsewhere.

;UseCreationTime Yes
;
; Yes - file age is based on creation time, No - on modification time.
; Creation time is supported on Windows and on Linux (via statx(2), if
; syscall.ph is available and the file system stores creation time).
; Otherwise modification time is used. Default: Yes.

;WaitForFileDays 3
;
; How many days to wait for a file that matches the tic by Crc and Size.
; After that see DeleteOrphanTics. Default: 3.

;DeleteOrphanTics No
;
; Yes - delete tics for which no matching file arrived in time, No - move
; them to DestPath without a file. Non-matching files are never touched.
; Default: No.

;WaitForHiddenTicDays 7
;
; Windows: how many days to skip a tic with the 'hidden' attribute (it may
; still be being received). After that it is processed as usual.
; 0 - do not wait. Files and tics moved to DestPath always have the
; attribute cleared. Default: 7.

;TouchFiles No
;
; Yes - set the current time on good files when moving them.
; Default: No.

;OverwriteExisting No
;
; Yes - overwrite files in DestPath and CorruptTicPath. No - if a file or
; tic with the same name is already there, skip the tic until the next
; run. Default: No.

;MaxTicSize 65536
;
; Tics larger than this size (in bytes) are considered corrupt.
; Default: 65536.

;CorruptTicAction Move
;
; What to do with corrupt tics (too large, binary, no File/Lfile, Size is
; not a number, file name with a path, drive letter, control characters,
; '.', '..' or a device name such as CON or NUL):
;   Move   - move to CorruptTicPath;
;   Delete - delete;
;   Keep   - leave in place (log only).
; Default: Move.

CorruptTicPath d:\fido\inbound\corrupt
;
; Where to move corrupt tics. Required with CorruptTicAction Move.
; Must be different from TicPath and FilesPath.

LogFile d:\fido\log\ticmambo.log
;
; Log file (UTF-8). If not set, the log goes to stderr.

;LogLevel info
;
; Log level: error, warn, info, debug. Default: info.
